{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.82,"content_digest":"13d48dca5b2fcf4a8341db976cbe02e3c90ae246043ebd97c6bfc6818403e16a","created_at":"2026-08-23T11:47:39+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"fa4ed750b2f7cc3dbc62d2a26b7ca1b67084ec245b8a6743794441f497d794a0","input_tokens":5954,"latency_ms":36251,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"562203419ff68bc6fab65e1014ba975c4cc5df47913bbed3285ff99d34a07f5c","output_tokens":2396,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:22804e7e2b23a7b9c14ecc14","meta_principle_id":"meta:mathematics-logic:invariance","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:physics:01M0Q744PBP657VXQTT8WA7M5E","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle is a specialization of the invariance meta-principle: it identifies a quantity (Fermi-level density of states) that remains unchanged under a declared transformation (renormalization scaling of Fermi velocity and quasiparticle weight by the same factor). The meta-principle's condition that an invariant is meaningful only relative to a transformation class is satisfied by the renormalized quasiparticle picture.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T11:47:39+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.82,"content_digest":"b5a8b89d2cc5a658bb03553b4824935fb13560b27ef0f212891f74a7a5f43213","created_at":"2026-08-23T12:40:32+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"a899d50b3cb91af0c3c68dfbf6bf5bf872f97ab21f8c2592cb7de8cbe71193ff","input_tokens":4075,"latency_ms":58268,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"6028836622a6296eac5348776bf9f4c1110c839e0852e9296946fa2afe0e0cee","output_tokens":2384,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:41527530609383ff4eb2a637","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:inductive-bias","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:socio-technical-systems:01M0QA49THCM1GDN0SYNQ4XX7E","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that finite training data do not determine behavior and that priors, architecture, or optimization biases are required for generalization. Reward-only PPO in the reported POMDP benchmarks lacks a prior favoring trace alignment, so it misses trace alignment; trace-prior or corrected-history objectives add task-appropriate inductive bias and better preserve price/bid distributions. This makes the validated principle a specific application of the general inductive-bias principle.","relation_type":"supports","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T12:40:32+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
